{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-grammar-everyday-actions/audio/main-ad6026fdf014.mp3","durationSec":114.384,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.54,"text":"You talk about your day with a friend."},{"start":2.08,"end":4.42,"text":"For things that happen often, use the present simple."},{"start":4.96,"end":5.8,"text":"Person, Verb."},{"start":6.22,"end":7.46,"text":"I, read every day."},{"start":7.84,"end":8.86,"text":"you, eat breakfast."},{"start":9.36,"end":10.8,"text":"we, walk to school on Mondays."},{"start":11.52,"end":12.86,"text":"they, play after school."},{"start":13.54,"end":16.88,"text":"Rule: After I, you, we and they, the verb stays the same."},{"start":17.5,"end":18.9,"text":"I do my homework after school."},{"start":19.36,"end":20.04,"text":"I like cats."},{"start":20.6,"end":21.26,"text":"We need water."},{"start":21.5,"end":22.16,"text":"I read books."},{"start":22.5,"end":23.02,"text":"I am ready."},{"start":23.62,"end":25.06,"text":"Like and need are verbs too."},{"start":25.72,"end":28.66,"text":"Ordinary verbs use do to ask and say no, not be."},{"start":28.66,"end":30.92,"text":"Watch out: Not I am read."},{"start":31.26,"end":32.02,"text":"Say I read."},{"start":32.58,"end":33.82,"text":"Two friends talk about home."},{"start":33.82,"end":36.7,"text":"Person, Do question, Short answers."},{"start":37.22,"end":40.18,"text":"you (only you), Do you read at home, Yes, I do."},{"start":40.48,"end":41.18,"text":"/ No, I don't."},{"start":41.6,"end":44.34,"text":"you (a group), Do you read at home, Yes, we do."},{"start":44.62,"end":45.38,"text":"/ No, we don't."},{"start":45.88,"end":48.3,"text":"they, Do they walk to school, Yes, they do."},{"start":48.7,"end":49.82,"text":"/ No, they don't."},{"start":50.36,"end":52.26,"text":"Rule: To ask, put do first."},{"start":52.88,"end":55.16,"text":"To say no, put do not before the verb."},{"start":55.62,"end":56.48,"text":"You read at home."},{"start":56.98,"end":57.82,"text":"Do you read at home?"},{"start":57.82,"end":59.34,"text":"I do not read at home."},{"start":59.8,"end":60.86,"text":"They don't walk to school."},{"start":60.86,"end":62.38,"text":"You means only you?"},{"start":62.8,"end":63.48,"text":"Answer with I."},{"start":64.08,"end":64.52,"text":"A group?"},{"start":65.08,"end":65.72,"text":"Answer with we."},{"start":66.54,"end":68.36,"text":"A question word comes first, then do."},{"start":69.16,"end":71.54,"text":"Question word, Asks about, Example."},{"start":72.26,"end":74,"text":"What, a thing, What do you read."},{"start":74.58,"end":77.1,"text":"Where, a place, Where do you eat lunch."},{"start":77.76,"end":80.44,"text":"When, a time, When do you read."},{"start":81.16,"end":82.92,"text":"Be is different: Are you ready?"},{"start":83.56,"end":85.22,"text":"Watch out: Not Are you read?"},{"start":85.74,"end":86.66,"text":"Say Do you read?"},{"start":86.66,"end":88.28,"text":"Your answer is no."},{"start":88.78,"end":90.64,"text":"Write do not or don't."},{"start":90.94,"end":92.16,"text":"Full form, Short form."},{"start":92.86,"end":94.42,"text":"I do not play, I don't play."},{"start":94.92,"end":96.66,"text":"They do not eat, They don't eat."},{"start":97.22,"end":99.82,"text":"Rule: Don't and do not mean the same thing."},{"start":100.18,"end":101.28,"text":"We do not walk to school."},{"start":101.88,"end":102.92,"text":"We don't walk to school."},{"start":103.42,"end":104.2,"text":"I don't like cats."},{"start":104.8,"end":105.34,"text":"Do you play?"},{"start":105.96,"end":106.74,"text":"No, I don't."},{"start":107.18,"end":109.14,"text":"In don't, the o from not is gone."},{"start":109.58,"end":110.84,"text":"The apostrophe is in its place."},{"start":111.58,"end":113.4,"text":"Watch out: Not dont."},{"start":113.4,"end":114.14,"text":"Say don't."}],"words":[{"text":"You","start":0,"end":0.24},{"text":"talk","start":0.24,"end":0.46},{"text":"about","start":0.46,"end":0.66},{"text":"your","start":0.